<!--
  Rounds Codex — Android App Links intent filter.

  CANONICAL SOURCE for the six deep-link prefixes on Android. Paste inside the
  <activity android:name=".MainActivity"> element of
  android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml, alongside (not replacing) the LAUNCHER filter that
  `npx cap add android` generates.

  This file is spec-derived, not project-derived: the six prefixes come from the route contract the
  web app already implements, so it is correct independently of what the Capacitor template looks
  like. `node scripts/verify_routes.js <web-clone>` asserts it stays in step with the other four
  sources — change a route in one place and that check fails.

  roundscodex.com ONLY. Do not add the netlify.app host: App Links verification requires
  /.well-known/assetlinks.json on the host, the apex is the canonical origin (RC_SHARE_ORIGIN), and
  a second unverifiable host makes Android give up on the whole filter.

  android:autoVerify="true" is what makes Android fetch assetlinks.json at install time. Without it
  the links still work but only via a disambiguation dialog, which most people dismiss.

  MainActivity is launchMode="singleTask" in the Capacitor template, so a link tapped while the app
  is already running arrives at onNewIntent rather than a fresh activity.
-->
<intent-filter android:autoVerify="true">
    <action android:name="android.intent.action.VIEW" />
    <category android:name="android.intent.category.DEFAULT" />
    <category android:name="android.intent.category.BROWSABLE" />
    <data android:scheme="https" android:host="roundscodex.com" />
    <data android:pathPrefix="/c/" />
    <data android:pathPrefix="/s/" />
    <data android:pathPrefix="/g/" />
    <data android:pathPrefix="/r/" />
    <data android:pathPrefix="/u/" />
    <data android:pathPrefix="/x/" />
</intent-filter>
